Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["From a Sullivan Model to an IBL Algebra", "Title",
 CellID->509267359,ExpressionUUID->"4ddb5767-1f00-4973-a411-49eacd07850d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The dIBL algebra of a closed oriented ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0de0a5cf-1662-4844-a3ac-fb54bee6cdfa"],
 "-manifold ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1c738c5b-2acc-47f5-ba6e-eb6ad16d0aba"],
 " lives on the cyclic words of a graded alphabet, and the alphabet is a \
basis of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "*"], "(", 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66fb5035-3633-4e1d-95ed-b99ecc8cf615"],
 " shifted by one, with the pairing that Poincar\[EAcute] duality gives it. \
This tutorial builds that alphabet without ever mentioning ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "046c5b59-704a-4477-bb6f-944636cc1057"],
 ": it starts from a Sullivan minimal model, puts the natural volume form on \
it, checks that the resulting oriented PDGA is of Hodge type, passes to the \
nondegenerate quotient, and reads the canonical Maurer-Cartan element off the \
triple product of the quotient. The running example is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["CP",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "be841e51-d75e-42c9-923b-b6df1b18a9e9"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ed2916ae-5b8d-4ad3-921f-0cb899397a7d"],

Cell["Five steps, and each one is a single function.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"82012fe3-0951-4898-bd03-1902bb7e1c98"],

Cell["The minimal model", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5fa92f5f-81dd-4cc1-a7f1-314b4602ea0d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A Sullivan minimal model is a free graded commutative algebra ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalLambda]", 
    StyleBox["U", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2bc9b694-9dfd-4056-a95c-7e00f82fa8fc"],
 " with a differential. For ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["CP",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "28f781d8-cde2-4314-84f5-dd4fc3a5b57d"],
 " it has two generators: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d57fd9e-d3e2-45e4-be44-eb8342fdecbc"],
 " in degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["2", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "913e5b55-14c3-473e-bb13-cd58a570de4b"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3ccdc5b8-625f-49c4-ad64-e54d78c89251"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fcf8d7b7-ff35-4354-aaf0-7d67895e9a65"],
 " in degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], "+", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09a90b6a-dd07-4a7b-832f-4b80ae70981f"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["m", "TI"], "+", "1"}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1bc94a28-31b9-4a56-8fae-1f9722337725"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e6e0e837-114f-4e38-a308-3358680adfe5"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"model", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"SullivanModel", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<ComplexProjectiveSpace\>\"", "[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
  RowBox[{"model", "[", "\"\<Generators\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"adb7c82a-cd5e-4011-bd34-d844e4cc1f6a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"a", "\[Rule]", "2"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"b", "\[Rule]", "5"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[1]= ",ExpressionUUID->"3de74448-4a9d-41eb-950c-e2fdbc288a3d"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The differential is stored on the generators and extended as a derivation. It \
raises degree by one:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5be5ba92-56cd-44a4-863f-5bde57d8a1c4"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"SullivanModelDifferential", "[", 
    RowBox[{"b", ",", " ", "model"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"SullivanModelDifferential", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"a", " ", "b"}], ",", " ", "model"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"e40cd255-2200-4c6b-803f-12dc10ed9301"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["a", "3"], ",", 
   SuperscriptBox["a", "4"]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[2]= ",ExpressionUUID->"6879aeba-f248-4498-9dff-6c8b8c04fdc1"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A monomial is written as a product of generators, read in the order the \
model declares them. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["SullivanModelBasis"]], 
    "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/SullivanModelBasis", "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "fdcf7542-e363-4712-8f93-1009d6b8445a"],
 " lists the monomials of one degree; the algebra is infinite-dimensional, \
one or two monomials in every degree from here up."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"679f9588-8c30-4718-bdbb-051054e04292"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"SullivanModelBasis", "[", 
    RowBox[{"model", ",", " ", "k"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "8"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"59e7f91f-5a9d-467e-8667-92e2bfe53508"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", "a", "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    SuperscriptBox["a", "2"], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", "b", "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    SuperscriptBox["a", "3"], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"a", " ", "b"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    SuperscriptBox["a", "4"], "}"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[3]= ",ExpressionUUID->"5ca6daff-a5c4-4031-943b-4ddc2c2d775d"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["The volume form, and the pairing it defines", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"065e50b3-e9f6-4c5f-8039-fa7fe287ea44"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The cohomology of this model is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["R",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "]"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "3"], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bff837a2-1d97-4669-b03e-17a3b33e7d4e"],
 ", so the top class is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6588b6d2-940b-44f9-b46b-05a1178794c6"],
 " in degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d64ef43a-c5c8-409f-b413-b655c86e76c9"],
 ". Take that monomial as the ",
 StyleBox["volume form", "TI"],
 " and let the orientation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "554d723c-2c0f-4289-8462-acdd3c8b095c"],
 " be the coefficient of it \[LongDash] the projection onto the volume form. \
That is what ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"model", "[", "\"\<Volume\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d6a311d9-e366-4ad3-a751-c41d52405a15"],
 " records, as the list of the generators of the monomial."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b238ea06-47fd-456b-904c-a7903151ebf2"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"model", "[", "\"\<Volume\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"model", "[", "\"\<Degree\>\"", "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"63da0ed2-fc8f-48bb-9454-2c1558d12751"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"a", ",", "a"}], "}"}], ",", "4"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[4]= ",ExpressionUUID->"de5e7e4e-1473-4e33-8a9b-b3b200cea135"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["SullivanModelOrientation"]], 
    "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/SullivanModelOrientation", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "e774ce1a-4a26-4af7-8753-97894c10d640"],
 " applies it. Everything outside degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "85f78198-cd48-4151-8be3-4cbedd282d9c"],
 " is killed, and inside degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9ad688d2-c4ef-425c-9160-9820cca83518"],
 " only the volume monomial survives:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f2a8cd36-18eb-43f7-bdea-f105e68d40e4"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"SullivanModelOrientation", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"a", "^", "2"}], ",", " ", "model"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"SullivanModelOrientation", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"a", "^", "3"}], ",", " ", "model"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"SullivanModelOrientation", "[", 
    RowBox[{"b", ",", " ", "model"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"0fcc8215-67bb-4eef-a8e8-5f7e46d6ff4b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"1", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[5]= ",ExpressionUUID->"d7a5822b-8442-4d65-bfa9-690c26d1d591"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The pairing is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[LeftAngleBracket]", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["v", "TI"], "1"], ",", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["v", "TI"], "2"]}], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
    
    StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["v", "TI"], "1"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["v", "TI"], "2"]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b05ca556-60e8-4326-a2f6-5f416358cfa5"],
 " \[LongDash] the projection of the product onto the volume form. On ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"1", ",", 
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], ",", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "2"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "641a1554-1af0-4f64-bd22-d40e428aae9c"],
 " it is the antidiagonal, which is Poincar\[EAcute] duality:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ac1c0caa-c166-4165-a488-01e9d838e27f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"SullivanModelPairing", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"a", "^", "i"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"a", "^", "j"}], ",", " ", "model"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"i", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "//", 
  " ", "MatrixForm"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"b538ebaa-123c-4999-a9bb-cfd9de1673d0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", GridBox[{
     {"0", "0", "1"},
     {"0", "1", "0"},
     {"1", "0", "0"}
    },
    GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Center}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {
        Offset[0.27999999999999997`], {
         Offset[0.7]}, 
        Offset[0.27999999999999997`]}, "Rows" -> {
        Offset[0.2], {
         Offset[0.4]}, 
        Offset[0.2]}}], "\[NoBreak]", ")"}],
  Function[BoxForm`e$, 
   MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[6]= ",ExpressionUUID->"352b8780-3272-4a58-96a7-0a1927599060"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is an ",
 StyleBox["orientation", "TI"],
 " in the sense of Lambrechts-Stanley: it has degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c478fd47-9835-418c-b4f0-b0caecef45b2"],
 ", it kills the image of the differential, and it does not vanish on the \
kernel. Together with the perfect pairing it induces on cohomology, that \
makes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalLambda]", 
     StyleBox["U", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["d",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], ",", 
     StyleBox["O", "TI"]}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7126ebc2-e8dc-4581-96eb-06681c1f7004"],
 " an oriented PDGA of degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "833ed72e-2d63-458a-a8e0-9d5ea14f5315"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b4e9c9da-de84-49a3-9078-a11f46a0b15b"],

Cell["Is it of Hodge type?", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d9d8269b-d652-4d3d-bdca-b3d5df66baf5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The pairing is ",
 StyleBox["not", "TI"],
 " perfect on chain level: the whole of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalLambda]", 
    StyleBox["U", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b3cdc446-8cc9-4750-9ee5-b3a987061877"],
 " above degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c5f0179f-acbf-482b-bc56-4e5abcbee47d"],
 " is paired to zero with everything, because the orientation only sees \
degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "59d1dbdd-6fd5-404b-815d-fac3aaa11c83"],
 ". Those elements form the ",
 StyleBox["degenerate subspace", "TI"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["deg",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1190ffbc-9892-440a-ada3-ac4aa8eaf92f"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"834a5f3c-5041-48d7-b258-6d3e8a282106"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"DegenerateSubspace", "[", 
    RowBox[{"model", ",", " ", "5"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"DegenerateSubspace", "[", 
    RowBox[{"model", ",", " ", "6"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"DegenerateSubspace", "[", 
    RowBox[{"model", ",", " ", "7"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"01cd53d7-9193-46e6-bcfd-be0d0daf8abf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "b", "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    SuperscriptBox["a", "3"], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"a", " ", "b"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[7]= ",ExpressionUUID->"b6632020-e4a2-4fcb-967e-d6bb750add50"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The oriented PDGA is ",
 StyleBox["of Hodge type", "TI"],
 " when it admits a Hodge decomposition ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], "\[CirclePlus]", 
    StyleBox["im",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
    StyleBox["d",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[CirclePlus]", 
    StyleBox["C", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "093c563e-db15-4bc6-afbb-1d242ec0a4c7"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["C", "TI"], "\[Perpendicular]", 
    StyleBox["C", "TI"], "\[CirclePlus]", 
    StyleBox["H", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "563d252c-b853-4fae-9f06-9c9aea5cffc4"],
 ". Over a field of characteristic ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[NotEqual]", "2"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "aa1f21a5-c6fb-41c3-830a-ef2997e9d3f9"],
 " and for a quotient of finite type, that happens exactly when ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["deg",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "89f17e1e-afa1-474d-b9ba-9c1ed752c504"],
 " is acyclic \[LongDash] equivalently, exactly when the quotient map onto \
the nondegenerate quotient is a quasi-isomorphism. So the test is one \
cohomology computation."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cb31d409-4092-436c-b758-cd76deb8e818"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"HodgeTypeQ", "[", "model", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"c31db2e4-d6af-4419-a141-d9611d8b581c"],

Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[8]= ",ExpressionUUID->"09aca227-10de-4ce3-a3ea-e4a6bc171052"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["HodgeTypeReport"]], "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/HodgeTypeReport", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "c49aee67-3041-4531-98a5-76635bcd1a99"],
 " shows why, degree by degree. The fourth column is the cohomology of the \
degenerate subspace, and it vanishes throughout. Here the second and fifth \
columns agree as well, which says more: the quotient carries no differential, \
so it ",
 StyleBox["is", "TI"],
 " the cohomology \[LongDash] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["CP",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ca7b291-1a9a-48d9-b9d6-4de3d069ff23"],
 " is formal. A Hodge-type model whose quotient keeps a differential has ",
 Cell[BoxData["Cohomology"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "49462cca-facb-4708-b836-95a5a57e5fad"],
 " strictly below ",
 Cell[BoxData["Quotient"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6a8183cb-fa1b-4793-b7b0-48a3c2278a62"],
 ", and the next tutorial shows one."
